fix(dsc): stop the directory scan dropping the tail of every window

The shared cache was not mapped because one subcache file was never seen:

    KEBAB DSC: subcache 38 suffix ".38" uuid 0f806d3d...: NO FILE WITH THIS UUID
    KEBAB DSC: resolved 37/42 subcaches by uuid; dylddata=1 dyldlinkedit=1

The file is installed and hash-verified, its own header carries that UUID,
and no "cannot open" or "not a dyld cache header" line was printed, so the
name was never offered to the resolver.  The cause is the scan's bound:

    while (pos + sizeof(struct dirent) <= used)

sizeof(struct dirent) is 1048 (d_name[1024]), which is the *largest* record
HFS+ can emit, so it is not a lower bound at all.  hfs_vnop_readdir() emits
variable-length records:

    STD_DIRENT_LEN(namlen) = (sizeof(struct dirent) - 256)
                             + ((namlen + 1 + 3) & ~3)

which is 816-836 bytes for the 44 names in this directory.  The bound
therefore stopped as soon as fewer than 1048 bytes remained, leaving the last
complete record of every 8 KiB window unread, and because the next
VNOP_READDIR resumed from the offset the driver reported, that name was
skipped permanently and silently.  44 entries fit 5 windows, so 5 names were
never offered -- the same count as the 5 subcaches that failed to resolve.

Bound the walk on the fixed header, offsetof(struct dirent, d_name), and
trust d_reclen after bounds-checking it: reclen >= DIRENT_MIN and
reclen <= used - pos, plus d_namlen + 1 <= reclen - DIRENT_MIN before the
name is copied out.

Make a partial scan loud instead of silent.  A remainder shorter than a
dirent header, a d_reclen that does not fit the window, or a readdir that
returns zero records without EOF now prints the offsets (pos, used,
d_reclen, readdir offset) and fails the plan, so a truncated candidate list
can never again look like a successful one.

Add the offered-versus-resolved accounting to the normal success line:

    KEBAB DSC: plan 43 files / 51 mappings, ..., dynamic config page absent;
               dir 44 entries, 44 offered, 44 resolved

and the same three numbers to the verbose detail line.  A directory that
loses a name is now visible without kebab_dsc_verbose=1.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c b/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c
@@ -84,6 +84,12 @@
 #define KEBAB_DSC_PATH_MAX              256
 #define KEBAB_DSC_NAME_MAX              64
 #define KEBAB_DSC_DIRBUF                8192
+/*
+ * Smallest record the scan can consume: the fixed part of a struct dirent,
+ * i.e. offsetof(struct dirent, d_name).  sizeof(struct dirent) is the largest
+ * record HFS+ can emit, not the smallest, so it must never bound the walk.
+ */
+#define KEBAB_DSC_DIRENT_MIN            ((uint32_t)offsetof(struct dirent, d_name))
 #define KEBAB_DSC_MAX_CANDIDATES        96
 #define KEBAB_DSC_MAX_SUBCACHES         64
 #define KEBAB_DSC_MAX_FILES             (1 + KEBAB_DSC_MAX_SUBCACHES)
@@ -283,6 +289,9 @@
 	uint32_t        subcache_count;
 	uint32_t        dylddata_count;
